      "summary": "During a campaign visit to the French overseas territory of Mayotte ahead of the 2027 presidential election, Édouard Philippe pledged to \"close the taps\" on immigration and address what he characterized as a pull factor drawing migrants to the region. His promises came as he met with local officials who have grown frustrated by unfulfilled commitments on immigration from previous administrations.",
      "takeaway": "A leading centrist-right candidate is adopting maximalist immigration rhetoric to appeal to voters in an overseas territory exhausted by years of uncontrolled migration.",
      "why_it_matters": "Édouard Philippe's campaign pledge to completely close immigration to Mayotte signals a hardening position on immigration policy within the Les Républicains party that will likely shape the 2027 presidential race and influence immigration debates across France's political spectrum."
